. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.     * Hypothesis: The effect of daughters on gender attitudes differs by resp
> ondent sex
.     * Model: 2SLS regression with interaction (prop_daughters × sex), instrum
> ented by first_child_female × sex
.     * Controls: dummies for total number of children, age squared, log of hou
> sehold income, born in germany, from east or west germany, years of education
. 
.     ivregress 2sls gendereq (prop_daughters prop_daughters_sex = ///
>         first_child_female first_child_female_sex) ///
>         partner germborn westgerm pgbilzeit age age_sq ln_hghinc kids_*, ///
>         vce(robust)
note: kids_0 omitted because of collinearity.
note: kids_8plus omitted because of collinearity.

